  "full_text": "Mr. God, how often were extinctions due to instability in the predator-prey equation? Like, the stability margins on the predator-prey. It's like, Mr. God, how often were extinctions due to instability? But that's a little bit shallow analysis. Because, like, anyway. But they hearken not nor incline their ear. but walked in the councils and the imaginations of their evil heart, and went backward and not forward. Oh, so like you pump up the, it's like, hey, start reproducing, and they like stop reproducing. Like, what the fuck? Since today your fathers came forth out of the land of Egypt unto this day, I have sent unto you all my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them, that they hearken not unto me, nor incline their ear, but harden their necks. They did worse than their fathers. Therefore, shall I speak these words unto them? Thou shalt say unto them, This is a nation that obeyed not the voice of the Lord, nor received correction. The truth is perished. It is cut off from their mouth. Cut off thine hair, O Jerusalem. Cast it away. Take a lamentation on the high places. The Lord has rejected and forsaken the generation of his wrath.",
